package kgen

func init() {
	opsEntries = append(opsEntries,
		opsDoc{"repl:PreventDamageFilt", "ReplPreventDamageFilt (Filter recipient, Filter2 source, C ReplSP* bits, A DamageAmount$ bound, Cond)",
			"Damage that would be dealt to a recipient the line names by a source it names is prevented, once per damage event (combat: once per source and recipient), after protection: no damage, no lifelink, no damage trigger; a can't-prevent static keeps it (CR 615.12). The recipient is a permanent matching Filter (relative to the host: YouCtrl, EnchantedBy, EquippedBy, Self), every permanent (ReplSPAnyPerm) or a player (ReplSPYou the host's controller, ReplSPOpp an opponent); Filter2 is the source (a permanent or a spell; ReplSPSrcSpell the resolving spell, ReplSPSrcInPlay a battlefield source); ReplSPCombat / ReplSPNonCombat (IsCombat$), ReplSPYourTurn (PlayerTurn$ True), ReplSPDmgLE (DamageAmount$ LE<A>), ReplSPRecipSnow (a printed Snow recipient), Cond (CheckSVar$, IsPresent$). Two or more matching full preventions apply with no order ask (gorge allBarePreventions); beside another candidate gorge asks the CR 616.1 order: a noncombat event parks on the ask (spPark), a combat event's orderable competition is posed by the combat walk (spCombatCands, with the pass's event aligned to the picked order), and a competition beside an optional line or a DamageAmount$ gate, or a host with two shields, stalls (StallReplPlus); the pair with any other damage replacement is refused at the game's start, except a SHIELD counter, which the walks pose last (spShieldLate). Bubble Matrix, Muzzle, Inviolability, Blessed Sanctuary, Statecraft, Personal Sanctuary."},
		opsDoc{"repl:PreventDamageN", "ReplPreventDamageN (the filters, bits and Cond of ReplPreventDamageFilt; A, V, C amount bits)",
			"Prevents min(N, the damage left) of each damage event it matches (DB$ ReplaceDamage | Amount$ N, CR 615.7); the event stands with the rest. N is A, V (ReplSPAmtV: a count read when the damage would be dealt), all but A of the damage (ReplSPAllBut: Hyperion, Temple Altisaur) or at most the host's counters of kind A (ReplSPLimitCtr: Rock Hydra, which gorge never removes the counters of). A shield is never a bare prevention, so two matching candidates are gorge's order ask: a noncombat event parks on the ask, a combat event's orderable competition is posed by the combat walk (each pick applies to the damage left, and the pass's event is aligned to the picked order), the last candidate applies on its own and a prevention that leaves nothing ends the asks. A competition beside an optional line or a DamageAmount$ gate, or a host with two shields, stalls (StallReplPlus). ReplSPOptional (Battletide Alchemist) is asked of its controller with a skip option, a noncombat lone candidate only. The six Spheres, Urza's Armor, Orbs of Warding, Guardian Seraph, Shield of the Realm, Plated Pegasus, Thunderstaff."},
	)
}
